  "weekLabel": "Week of Nov 9–13, 2026",
  "headline": "vVardis and Rezera bring ~$414M to market as Anthropic's launch hangs on a shaky AI tape",
  "summary": "Two sizable deals are on the Nov 9–13 calendar: Boston NLRP3 biotech Rezera (RZRA, Nasdaq) plans to raise $200M at $11–$13 and is set to trade Thu, Nov 12, and Swiss cavity-treatment maker vVardis (VVVV, NYSE) plans $214M at $21–$24, pricing Nov 12 for a Fri, Nov 13 debut at about a $1.35B market cap. Anthropic amended its S-1 on Nov 2 but still hasn't set a price range; Renaissance says it could launch as early as Tue, Nov 10 for pricing the week of Nov 16, and the FT reports a $80B–$100B raise at a $1.25T–$1.75T valuation before Thanksgiving, though Reuters says some investors doubt the roadshow can start next week after the post-midterm AI selloff. Last week was quiet: Narragansett Bancorp (NARA) closed its $91M offering at $10 and is up 8.4%, while Football Manager SPAC and Bitari slipped to later weeks on IPOScoop. Of the Oct 30 debuts, Aspen Neuroscience (ASPE) is down 17.1% and Bambusa (BBTX) 1.7% as of Nov 6. New filings were small: three SPACs (including Churchill Capital XIV at $300M) and three micro-caps.",
  "highlights": [
    {
      "text": "Rezera (RZRA) plans a $200M Nasdaq IPO at $11–$13, expected to trade Thu, Nov 12",
      "unconfirmed": false
    },
    {
      "text": "vVardis (VVVV) plans a $214M NYSE IPO at $21–$24, pricing Nov 12 and trading Fri, Nov 13",
      "unconfirmed": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Anthropic (ANT) could launch as soon as Tue, Nov 10 for pricing the week of Nov 16; FT reports an $80B–$100B raise at $1.25T–$1.75T",
      "unconfirmed": true,
      "note": "No terms filed; Reuters reports investor doubts about the timing"
    },
    {
      "text": "Narragansett Bancorp (NARA) is up 8.4% from its $10 offering price after its Nov 2 debut",
      "unconfirmed": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Churchill Capital XIV (CXIVU) filed for a $300M SPAC IPO; DT House and GLAMOORE withdrew small IPOs",
      "unconfirmed": false
    }
  ],
